ScanSafe.AI — Complete App Flow and Application Logic
The goal is to turn your screen designs into a working Android application where every button, scan, API request, loading indicator, error message and result has a defined behavior.

The core principle is: every screen must be connected to real application logic, and every operation must have success, loading, empty, error and recovery behavior wherever applicable.

I'll structure this around your 32-screen inventory and your existing ScanSafe.AI visual direction.

1. Overall application flow
1. Launch

Splash → onboarding if needed

2. Session and permissions

Guest or signed-in state · camera permission when scanning

3. Home Dashboard

Search · Scan · History · Saved · Profile

4. Scan workflow

Camera / Gallery → Crop → OCR → Review and correct ingredients

5. Analyze

Normalize ingredients → match database → retrieve evidence → evaluate rules → validate report

6. Results

Findings · unknown ingredients · evidence · limitations

7. Follow-up actions

View details · save · share · report an issue · rescan

The Home Dashboard remains the central navigation point. Users should be able to leave a scan, return to it safely, or recover from a failed request without having to restart the entire process.

2. Detailed flow for the primary scan journey
1
Start scanning

User taps Scan. Check camera permission, account/guest policy and scan quota.

2
Capture or import

Open CameraX or the system photo picker. Allow retake, crop and alignment.

3
Validate image

Check file type, dimensions, size and readability. Reject unsupported or unusable images with a recovery action.

4
Extract text

Run OCR on-device where practical. Show progress only while work is actually running.

5
Review ingredients

Display extracted text for correction. Keep the original OCR result and the user's corrected version separately.

6
Submit analysis

Send confirmed text to the backend. Create an idempotent analysis job and show its real status.

7
Build report

Match ingredients, retrieve reviewed evidence and apply deterministic rules. Validate the report before saving.

8
Present findings

Show the report, matched and unmatched ingredients, evidence sources, region and limitations.

